LOG FETCHER TOOL – USER MANUAL

1. Introduction
The Log Fetcher Tool is a command-line automation utility designed to simplify and standardize log collection from Android-based automotive systems.
It integrates screen recording, bug report generation, log extraction, and packaging into a single workflow, eliminating manual effort and ensuring consistency across testing activities.
2. Purpose
•	Automate the process of collecting logs from the device
•	Reduce manual intervention during debugging
•	Ensure all required logs are captured in a structured format
•	Provide a ready-to-share ZIP file for analysis
3. Scope
Applicable for automotive infotainment and ADAS testing environments using Android-based systems.
•	Screen recording during test execution
•	Bugreport generation
•	Logcat capture
•	System log extraction (HS Logs, Maker Logs, MCU)
•	ZIP packaging (excluding video)
4. Benefits
•	Eliminates repetitive manual work
•	Ensures consistent folder structure
•	Saves ~70–80% time
•	Reduces chances of missing logs
•	Improves debugging efficiency
5. Initial Setup
System Requirements:
•	Windows OS
•	ADB installed and configured
•	PowerShell available
Device Requirements:
•	USB Debugging enabled
•	Device connected via USB
Tool Configuration:
•	Verify scrcpy path: D:\adb 1\adb\scrcpy.exe
6. User Interface
The tool uses a command-line interface with minimal user interaction such as entering folder name and controlling recording.
7. Procedure (Steps to Use the Tool)
Step 1: Open File Explorer and navigate to tool location
Step 2: Open ADB folder and verify required files
Step 3: Double-click Log and Video Recorder Tool.bat
Step 4: Enter defect/test name when prompted
Step 5: Connect device and ensure USB debugging is enabled
Step 6: Press any key to start recording
Step 7: Perform test scenario
Step 8: Press any key to stop recording
Step 9: Logs are collected automatically
Step 10: Verify logs and ZIP file in created folder
Step 11: Share ZIP file for analysis
8. Output Structure
Example:
Test2/
 ├── Test2.zip
 ├── Video/
 ├── Bugreport/
 ├── Logcat/
 ├── HS_Logs/
 ├── Maker_Logs/
 └── MCU/
Final Note
This tool standardizes log collection and improves efficiency, enabling faster debugging and better collaboration.
